Track 2: Platform 4 Ticket-Puncher’s Lament
- Story & Context: In the blistering midday heat of the abandoned junction, retired ticket-puncher Kenji sat on an overturned mango crate, methodically running his copper hole-punch along the edges of brittle magnetic tape ribbon to turn our last surviving time-capsule recording into an unreadable lace of rhythm. His fingers reeked of coconut oil and machine grease as he confessed he had forged every arrival log since 1941 just to keep the islanders waiting for a train that had already dissolved into the reef. Sora leaned over his shoulder, plucking a weeping minor-third Hirajōshi bend on her koto that resonated inside an empty oil drum, before Kenji whispered through the megaphone, "My pockets are heavy with punched-out hours."
