Track 3: The 05:40 Departed Backward
- Story & Context: Legend says that when the guild finally played the repaired tape's final spool, the rusted clock hands on the terminal wall spun furiously counter-clockwise until the salt-crusted rails began to sing in perfect fifths. Three hundred dancers in guava-colored linen locked arms on the boardwalk as a spectral brass section appeared through the heat mirage, blowing swing licks so hot they melted the paraffin wax right out of the boardwalk planks. By the time the train finally pulled out in reverse toward the horizon, the koto strings had snapped one by one into the sea breeze, leaving Sora screaming the final refrain to the empty sky: "Cancel the calendar, we missed the end of the world!"
